.TH SYSLOG\-RELAY 1 "2026-11-05" "unheaded 31956da1" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
syslog\-relay \- Receive syslog over UDP and TCP and write it to the local journal (ADR\-124).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syslog\-relay
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Receive syslog over UDP and TCP and write it to the local journal (ADR\-124).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-accept\-unknown
ship unknown senders as source unknown; for the inventory phase only
.TP
.B \-\-burst \fIN\fR
token bucket size per sender; a row's burst: lowers it (default 1000)
.TP
.B \-\-idle\-timeout \fIDURATION\fR
time a TCP sender has to complete a frame (default 5m0s)
.TP
.B \-\-journal\-socket \fISTRING\fR
the journal's native socket (default /run/systemd/journal/socket)
.TP
.B \-\-listen \fIVALUE\fR
udp://IP:PORT or tcp://IP:PORT, repeatable; required, no wildcard address
.TP
.B \-\-max\-conns \fIN\fR
TCP connections at once, across every listener (default 256)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-conns\-per\-sender \fIN\fR
TCP connections one sender may hold, below \-\-max\-conns; 0 means a sixteenth of it
.TP
.B \-\-max\-msg \fIN\fR
message cap in bytes; longer is truncated and flagged (default 8192)
.TP
.B \-\-metrics \fIVALUE\fR
address for /metrics, /health and /ready, repeatable (default 127.0.0.1:9599)
.TP
.B \-\-rate \fIN\fR
messages per second per sender; a row's rate: lowers it (default 200)
.TP
.B \-\-sources \fISTRING\fR
sources file (config/logging/sources.yaml) (default config/logging/sources.yaml)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH NOTES
Senders are the kind: syslog\-device rows of the sources file that are not excluded; a match is <ip> or
<ip> <tag>. Others are counted and dropped. SIGHUP reloads the sources file; a bad file keeps the old list.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
syslog\-relay \-\-listen udp://10.10.20.1:514 \-\-listen tcp://10.10.20.1:514 \-\-sources /etc/unheaded/log\-sources.yaml
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
